  "contract_clause_fired": "expanded_after_distortion -> NONUNIFORM_SCALING. Contract v2 added this from the owner rule: \"geometry expanded only after distortion to conceal the transform\" is category B PROHIBITED.",
  "interpretation_tension": "This mandate section 4 defines the prohibited case as a glyph \"carrying an ACTIVE non-uniform transform\". These outlines were baked, so no active transform matrix survives in the delivered file. Under that narrower wording the submission would pass; under the frozen contract clause it does not. The two readings disagree and only the owner can settle it. Reported rather than silently resolved.",
